      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this is flawed because it makes implicit assumptions about the node order within the input DT.\n\nWhy wouldn\u0027t pvmfw follow what the kernel does i.e.\n```\nfor cpu in cpu_nodes.by_ref().take(cpus.capacity()) {\n    let opp_phandle \u003d cpu_node.getprop_u32(cstr!(\"operating-points-v2\"))?;\n    let opptable_info \u003d if let Some(phandle) \u003d opp_phandle {\n        let phandle \u003d phandle.try_into()?;\n        let node \u003d fdt.node_with_phandle(phandle)?.ok_or(FdtError::...)?;        \n        Some(read_opp_info_from(node)?)\n    } else {\n        None\n    };\n\n    let info \u003d CpuInfo { opptable_info };\n```\n(the encapsulation could be reworked but you get the idea about the DT parsing)\n\nNote that this isn\u0027t necessary for `patch_` (as the platform DT is compiled along with this code so implicit assumptions about its layout are fine) but would have avoided the off-by-one bug it currently has.",
