      "writtenOn": "2024-02-07T15:15:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t you have an off-by-one bug because of L246 as\n\n- `(n \u003d\u003d 0)` --\u003e `node.ok_or(...)?.next_compatible(compat)?`\n- `(n \u003d\u003d 1)` --\u003e `node.ok_...?.next_...?.ok_...?.next_...?`\n- ...\n\nand as you call this function with the first compatible node of the tree?\n\nAFAICT, `cpu@X` then gets the OPPs of `cpu@(X-1)`, right?\n\nI\u0027d recommend implementing this function as\n```\nfn get_nth_compatible\u003c\u0027a\u003e(fdt: \u0026\u0027a mut Fdt, n: usize, compat: \u0026CStr) -\u003e Result\u003c\u003cOption\u003cFdtNodeMut\u003c\u0027a\u003e\u003e\u003e {\n    let mut node \u003d fdt.root_mut()?.next_compatible(compat)?;\n    for _ in 0..n {\n        node \u003d node.ok_or(FdtError::NoSpace)?.next_compatible(compat)?;\n    }\n    Ok(node)\n}\n```\n\nNote these other differences:\n\n1. The lifetime of `compat` (`\u0026CStr`) isn\u0027t tied to the lifetime of the `Fdt` (`\u0027a`);\n1. `n` is a `usize` instead of `i32`, similar to `Iterator::take()`.\n\nFinally, would you mind adding\n```\n// TODO(ptosi): Rework FdtNodeMut and replace this function.\n```\n?",
